# Snyk policy file — https://docs.snyk.io/manage-risk/policies
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS HERE AND NOT AT THE REPO ROOT
#
# There are two Snyk policy files in this repo and they are not interchangeable:
#
#   /.snyk                          SAST (`snyk code test`), which runs from the
#                                   repo root with no --file. Root is where it
#                                   looks; that file holds a code exclusion.
#   /sportspress-league-manager/    SCA (`snyk test --file=sportspress-league-
#     .snyk                         manager/package.json`). Despite running from
#                                   the repo root, Snyk resolves the policy
#                                   beside the TARGET MANIFEST, not the cwd.
#
# This was verified, not assumed: with this policy at the repo root the adm-zip
# ignore below is silently ignored and the scan stays red. Move it and the whole
# reason for the file disappears with no error message. Keep it next to
# package.json.
#
# Every entry MUST carry an `expires` date. An ignore that never lapses is a
# decision nobody revisits; a dated one forces the question again on a known
# day. When an entry expires the scan turns red again — that is the point, and
# the fix is to re-evaluate, not to extend it reflexively.
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-ADMZIP-19276676:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Symlink Attack in adm-zip@0.6.0, reachable only through
          @wordpress/scripts (wp-env). Snyk reports no upgrade or patch at any
          version, so this cannot be resolved by bumping a dependency.

          Not shipped: adm-zip is dev-only (`dev: true` in package-lock.json),
          and .distignore strips /node_modules, package.json and
          package-lock.json from the packaged plugin — the distributed artifact
          is the compiled build/ bundle. The production dependency set is three
          @dnd-kit packages, which is why the production-only npm-audit job
          passes while this scan does not.

          Not exploitable here: the attack requires extracting a hostile
          archive. adm-zip is invoked by wp-env against archives it downloads
          from WordPress.org during local environment setup, never against
          user-supplied input, and never at runtime on a WordPress site.

          Revisit on expiry: check whether @wordpress/scripts has moved off
          adm-zip or a patched release exists. If neither, re-date this entry
          with a fresh assessment rather than removing the expiry.
        expires: 2026-12-03T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-04T00:00:00.000Z
patch: {}
